---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Custom Web Application Development | Kelp Agency"
  description="Kelp designs and develops custom web applications, dashboards, and business workflows that connect with the systems your team already uses."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Custom Application Development"
    title="Applications Built Around Your Business"
    description="When your team is stuck stitching together spreadsheets, inboxes, and SaaS workarounds, custom software starts to make sense. We build web applications around your workflow so operations become clearer, faster, and easier to scale."
    lottieFile="content-creation.json"
  />

  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Most businesses start with existing tools, and that is usually the right
        move. The problem comes later when those tools stop fitting the workflow
        and the team starts compensating with manual steps, duplicate entry, and
        disconnected systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        At that point, the business is spending energy working around the
        software instead of using software to remove friction.
      </p>

      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        Custom applications make sense when the workflow matters enough to
        deserve its own system. We build around how your team actually works so
        the platform supports the operation instead of constantly interrupting
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we actually build</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Internal tools that replace manual or repetitive processes</li>
        <li>Dashboards that surface real-time business data</li>
        <li>Systems that connect multiple platforms into a single workflow</li>
        <li>Customer-facing tools that improve experience and accessibility</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Every application is different, but the goal is consistent: create a
        system that is reliable, maintainable, and built to scale with your
        business.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Custom web applications</li>
        <li>Internal dashboards and admin tools</li>
        <li>API integrations and system connections</li>
        <li>Data visualization and reporting interfaces</li>
        <li>Performance-focused, device-agnostic builds</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we approach it</h2>
      <p>
        We don’t start with technology—we start with structure. Understanding
        how your business operates determines what should be built, how it
        should function, and what success looks like.
      </p>

      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Define the system:</strong> Identify gaps, inefficiencies, and
          opportunities in your current workflow.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Map the structure:</strong> Outline how data, users, and
          actions should interact.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Design the interface:</strong> Create clear, usable
          experiences based on real use cases—not assumptions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Build and integrate:</strong> Develop the application and
          connect it to the systems you already use.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Refine and scale:</strong> Improve performance, expand
          functionality, and support long-term growth.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Define the Work Before Choosing the Technology</h2>
      <p>
        We begin with users, decisions, data, and exceptions. Who enters
        information? What has to be approved? Which system owns the final
        record? What should happen when an API fails or a user changes an order?
        Those answers shape the product, not the other way around.
      </p>
      <h2>Build Around the Actual Workflow</h2>
      <p>
        Possible work includes customer portals, internal tools, product
        configurators, dashboards, data interfaces, and API connections. We
        prototype critical paths, develop the application, connect it to
        existing systems, and plan for maintenance after launch. A smaller
        focused tool can be more valuable than a large platform that nobody can
        use easily.
      </p>
      <h2>An Example of a Real Integration</h2>
      <p>
        For <a href="/work/us-labels/">US Labels</a>, Kelp rebuilt a custom label designer and connected
        WooCommerce orders to Windows printing software through a dedicated
        Node.js and Express service. The customer interface and production
        workflow were part of the same project. For <a href="/work/artisan-talent/">Artisan Talent</a>, Kelp worked
        across WordPress, an Angular jobs application, and HubSpot pages to
        create a consistent experience for applicants.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your business has a process held together by spreadsheets, duplicate
        entry, or a collection of disconnected tools, walk us through it. We
        will help decide whether to configure an existing platform, connect what
        you have, or build something custom.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Workflow mapping and product requirements</li>
        <li>Prototype and interface design</li>
        <li>Custom application and API development</li>
        <li>Deployment, documentation, and support plan</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring a real example of the work from start to finish, including the
        awkward exception. We can assess whether a custom application,
        integration, or better use of an existing tool is the right response.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Does every workflow need a custom app?</h3>
      <p>
        No. We first consider configuration and integration. Custom software is
        most valuable when the business process cannot be supported well by
        available tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Application
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={75} />
  </div>

  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
